  "chemical_rationale": {
    "electrophile": "The authoritative PRE graph is N3-C13(=O1)-C14=C15. Cys-SG attacks beta carbon C15; the POST S-C15 bond and restored PRE C14=C15 bond establish a conjugate Michael-addition event.",
    "family": "This is an N-substituted acrylamide (more specifically an N-acryloyl azetidine) alpha,beta-unsaturated amide Michael acceptor, so the reaction-family semantic recommendation names Cys-SG addition at the beta carbon.",
    "independent_sample_assignment": "Recommend APPROVE because source identity/SHA, unique exact endpoints, supported model atom inventory, authoritative PRE graph and charges, raw-source POST geometry, role partition, and leakage evidence all pass; this recommendation creates no authority.",
    "n3_role_tradeoff": "N3 is chemically the amide nitrogen and is necessary to identify the electrophile as an amide rather than a generic enone. Under the CovaPIE role-partition contract, however, the compact reaction-center warhead may end at carbonyl C13; N3 is also the azetidine linker-side ring atom. Keeping N3 in linker gives one coherent four-atom warhead and one N3-C13 linker-warhead boundary.",
    "role_partition": "Exact4 {C13,O1,C14,C15} contains the carbonyl and conjugated alkene reaction center. The complete azetidine ring {C11,C16,N3,C12} is a coherent linker between scaffold N2 and warhead C13; every retained heavy atom is assigned exactly once.",
    "scope": "EXACT_CHEMISTRY_SIGNATURE_REUSABLE is limited to later candidates with the same approved full PRE graph, charges, reactive map, roles, boundary, seed, and anchors. It does not authorize all acrylamides or any cross-signature propagation.",
    "seed_and_anchors": "The accepted seed set is {N2,C10,C17}; primary N2 is the unique scaffold-side boundary atom and C10/C17 are its two first-shell scaffold neighbors. On the authoritative PRE scaffold-induced graph, C10 and C17 have the same canonical equivalence rank (4) and are exchanged by a label-preserving graph automorphism. The published owners expose no input-numbering-independent secondary tie-break. Direction/plane labels therefore require a human convention choice between exactly two equivalent options; no linker, warhead, POST coordinate, or reactive-geometry information may break the tie.",
    "smarts": "The SMARTS encodes C13(=O1)-C14=C15 with the published atom maps, matches exactly once, and includes reactive C15/map30. It intentionally omits N3 so its match set equals the reviewed Exact4 role; amide identity is supplied by the full exact-signature PRE graph."
  },
